1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,200
When water becomes the single greatest threat to agriculture,

2
00:00:04,299 --> 00:00:08,800
billions of dollars in global crop yields are lost overnight.

3
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:12,199
Across millions of agricultural fields worldwide,

4
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:16,800
unpredictable rainfall and poorly drained terrain trigger severe waterlogging,

5
00:00:16,899 --> 00:00:20,949
suffocating root systems and transforming fertile soil into unproductive floodplains.

6
00:00:21,750 --> 00:00:27,949
Traditional drainage planning relies on slow, expensive manual surveying and guesswork.

7
00:00:28,050 --> 00:00:32,149
Subtle elevation depressions, invisible to the human eye,

8
00:00:32,250 --> 00:00:36,549
trap surface runoff, forming stagnant hydrological sinks.

9
00:00:36,649 --> 00:00:41,549
Without precision topographic modeling, surface runoff flows uncontrollably,

10
00:00:41,649 --> 00:00:46,280
accelerating topsoil erosion and devastating seasonal harvests.

11
00:00:47,079 --> 00:00:52,879
Introducing the Smart Agricultural Drainage & Precision Land Grading System.

12
00:00:52,979 --> 00:00:58,280
A unified, AI-driven geospatial intelligence platform developed at UEM Jaipur,

13
00:00:58,379 --> 00:01:03,280
engineered to transform satellite elevation data into actionable, millimeter-precise drainage networks

14
00:01:03,379 --> 00:01:06,709
and optimal land-grading strategies.

15
00:01:07,509 --> 00:01:13,309
By fusing high-resolution digital elevation models with Gaussian spatial filtering

16
00:01:13,409 --> 00:01:16,009
and numerical gradient analysis,

17
00:01:16,109 --> 00:01:22,309
the system constructs an interactive three-dimensional digital twin of any agricultural field.

18
00:01:22,409 --> 00:01:27,309
Topographic curvature algorithms locate localized depression sinks

19
00:01:27,409 --> 00:01:31,009
and identify natural watershed divide boundaries.

20
00:01:31,109 --> 00:01:36,009
Gravitational flow vectors reveal the exact trajectory of surface runoff,

21
00:01:36,109 --> 00:01:41,309
while a multi-catchment heuristic A* pathfinding engine autonomously computes

22
00:01:41,409 --> 00:01:44,009
the mathematically optimal routes for agricultural drainage trenches,

23
00:01:44,109 --> 00:01:46,049
minimizing excavation depth while maintaining continuous downhill flow.

24
00:01:46,849 --> 00:01:50,049
Inside the live interactive dashboard,

25
00:01:50,149 --> 00:01:56,649
farmers and agronomists can delineate field boundaries or select preset research plots with a single click.

26
00:01:56,750 --> 00:02:00,649
The platform instantly analyzes ground elevation profiles

27
00:02:00,750 --> 00:02:06,349
and highlights waterlogging vulnerability across critical, moderate, and well-drained zones.

28
00:02:06,449 --> 00:02:11,650
Users can toggle between existing terrain and laser-graded design surfaces,

29
00:02:11,750 --> 00:02:15,049
run real-time 3D rainfall inundation simulations,

30
00:02:15,150 --> 00:02:20,050
model SCS curve number runoff kinetics under dynamic soil saturation,

31
00:02:20,149 --> 00:02:26,069
and receive instant, crop-specific agronomic advisories powered by generative AI.

32
00:02:26,870 --> 00:02:32,370
Under the hood, the system features a high-performance decoupled architecture.

33
00:02:32,469 --> 00:02:38,069
A modern Next.js 14 frontend renders dynamic Three.js WebGL terrain meshes

34
00:02:38,170 --> 00:02:41,370
alongside responsive Leaflet GIS maps.

35
00:02:41,469 --> 00:02:46,670
The FastAPI Python backend powers high-throughput hydrological computing

36
00:02:46,770 --> 00:02:53,370
using NumPy vectorization, SciPy spatial filters, and custom least-squares planar grading,

37
00:02:53,469 --> 00:02:59,770
seamlessly integrated with Google Gemini AI for expert agronomic intelligence.

38
00:03:00,569 --> 00:03:06,069
From uncontrolled inundation to automated, precision-guided drainage.

39
00:03:06,169 --> 00:03:11,069
From manual surveying to autonomous geospatial intelligence.

40
00:03:11,169 --> 00:03:17,069
This is the future of sustainable farming and climate-resilient water management.

41
00:03:17,169 --> 00:03:22,370
Smarter Terrain. Intelligent Drainage. Better Agriculture.

42
00:03:22,469 --> 00:03:28,649
A Final-Year B.Tech Capstone Project, University of Engineering & Management, Jaipur.
